{"thought":"I understand the data structure. I need to find patients with Thrombosis = 2 (severe) from Examination table and join with Patient table to get their ID, SEX, and Diagnosis. Let me write a Python script to process this.","action":"execute_python","action_input":{"code":"import json\n\n# Read Patient data\nwith open('json/Patient.json', 'r') as f:\n    patient_data = json.load(f)\n\n# Read Examination data\nwith open('json/Examination.json', 'r') as f:\n    exam_data = json.load(f)\n\n# Create a dictionary of patients by ID for quick lookup\npatient_dict = {p['ID']: p for p in patient_data['records']}\n\n# Find patients with severe thrombosis (Thrombosis = 2)\nresult = []\nfor exam in exam_data['records']:\n    if exam.get('Thrombosis') == 2:\n        pid = exam['ID']\n        if pid in patient_dict:\n            patient = patient_dict[pid]\n            result.append({\n                'ID': pid,\n                'SEX': patient.get('SEX', ''),\n                'Diagnosis': patient.get('Diagnosis', '')\n            })\n\nprint(f\"Found {len(result)} patients with severe thrombosis\")\nfor r in result[:10]:\n    print(r)\nif len(result) > 10:\n    print(f\"... and {len(result)-10} more\")"}}
